<title>USA: Summa Four Q3 shr $0.08 vs $0.10.</title>
<headline>Summa Four Q3 shr $0.08 vs $0.10.</headline>
<dateline>MANCHESTER, N.H. 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>SUMMA FOUR, INC.</p>
<p>		    (In thousands, except per share amounts)</p>
<p>				Three Months Ended  Nine Months Ended</p>
<p>					     December 31,  December 31,</p>
<p>					  1996     1995    1996    1995</p>
<p> Net revenues		     $11,624 $10,321 $32,795 $29,958</p>
<p> Cost of revenues		   4,906   3,559  13,004  10,384</p>
<p> Gross profit			 6,718   6,762  19,791  19,574</p>
<p>Operating expenses</p>
<p>Selling, general and administrative  </p>
<p>					  3,714   3,268  10,795   9,583</p>
<p>  Research and development	2,500   2,677   7,528   6,542</p>
<p>  Total operating expenses	6,214   5,945  18,323  16,125</p>
<p> Operating income		     504     817   1,468   3,449</p>
<p> Interest income			234     232     783   1,105</p>
<p> Income before taxes		  738   1,049   2,251   4,554</p>
<p> Provision for income taxes	 281     399     855   1,732</p>
<p> Net income			     457     650   1,396   2,822</p>
<p> Net income per share		0.08    0.10    0.23    0.44</p>
<p> Weighted average common and    6,050   6,273   6,184   6,374</p>
<p>common equivalent shares outstanding  </p>
<p>Note: (*) A portion of customer service ($148,000) and research and development ($56,000) expenses were reclassified to cost of revenues for the quarter ended December 31, 1995.</p>
<p>In addition, corporate quality expenses of $57,000  were reclassified from cost of revenues to selling, general and administrative expenses. These reclassifications had no effect on operating or net income.</p>
<p>-- ((New York newsdesk 212-859-1611))</p>
